You can apply a Retention Policy to folders in Outlook so emails in that folder are automatically deleted or archived after a certain time. The steps depend on whether your organization (Microsoft 365 / Exchange) already created retention tags.
Method 1: Apply Retention Policy to a Folder (Outlook Desktop)
Open Microsoft Outlook.
In the left navigation pane, locate the folder (for example: Inbox subfolder).
Right-click the folder.
Click Properties.
Go to the Policy tab.
In Folder Policy, select the retention policy (example: Delete after 1 year, Archive after 2 years).
Click Apply → OK.
📌 This policy will apply to all emails inside that folder automatically.
Method 2: Apply Retention Policy to Individual Emails
Select the email(s).
Go to Home tab.
Click Assign Policy.
Choose the retention tag.
Method 3: Outlook Web (OWA)
Open Outlook on the Web.
Right-click the folder.
Select Assign policy.
Choose the retention policy.
✅ Example:
If you select Delete after 1 year, all emails in that folder will be automatically deleted after 1 year.
💡 Important:
If you don’t see retention policies, your Microsoft 365 admin must create them in
Microsoft Purview → Data lifecycle management → Retention policies.
